# Spring Boot 4 loads EnvironmentPostProcessor implementations from THIS file, under THIS
# key — not from META-INF/spring/*.imports (that mechanism is auto-configuration's) and
# not under the org.springframework.boot.env.* FQN that still exists as a deprecated
# alias. Registering it the wrong way is SILENT: the class compiles, ships, and simply
# never runs, and because an un-armed 007 is indistinguishable from a correctly inert one
# (onFail="CONTINUE"), nothing in a boot log would say so. DerivedRestampTargetBootTest is
# the assertion that catches it.
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
net.hugmesh.wikibff.config.RestampTargetEnvironmentPostProcessor
